WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.000
What the hell happened?

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.290
Did we all just lose?

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.450
That's right.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.750
Unfortunately, you've all stepped right into my trap.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.120
Nice to meet you, Ryuuou-kun.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.120
I've just taken possession of all of your slaves.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:26.330
Just as I expected, you became the perfect specimens
for collecting data on SCM usage.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:33.540
Thank you so much for dancing
so diligently in the palm of my hand.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:38.290
Sucks to be you, Fatass.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.620
All of you are gonna be my slaves.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:54.450
I want a heart that can laugh without lying

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:06.160
If I hadn't wanted anything from the start

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:13.870
Maybe my heart wouldn't have sank so low

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:22.750
I know the joy of being loved

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:31.330
But it's not enough, it won't fill me up, it won't purge my fears

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:37.290
Won't you wet my bone-dry heart?

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:41.080
Pour the oil over it till it's overflowing

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:46.660
My scream echoes out in vain

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:52.870
I want to feel that this boring everyday life

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:56.540
Is a blessing bestowed upon me

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:09.000
I want a heart that can laugh without lying

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:20.000
-harvest-

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.000
Judgement SCM?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.040
Yes.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.580
That's the star-symbol SCM

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.120
that Tsubaki Setagaya possesses.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.160
How is it different from a normal SCM?

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:32.660
Well, the Judgement SCM
can make people its slaves without a duel.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.620
Without a duel?

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.200
How to Deal With the Judgement (J) SCM
ABOUT THE JSCM:
- Black
- only one
- Biology Professor
- on GPS as star mark
- single
- no duels?
- nickname "Tsubakin"

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:37.250
That can't be possible.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.410
That's the only way I can explain it.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:45.000
Setagaya came to me one day after Minami enslaved me.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.910
The second he snapped his fingers...

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:57.830
...I heard the sound of a duel starting,
and I lost without even doing anything.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:03.540
Setagaya ordered me to pretend I was Minami's slave.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:07.750
Seemed he didn't want her to know
that he'd stolen me from her.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.040
He can make people his slaves without dueling them?

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.500
How are we supposed to win against someone like that?

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.750
Right, Eia?

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:18.080
An invincible SCM...

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.450
I sure don't like the sound of that.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:27.250
Nerima-san, did Setagaya give you
any other orders after he enslaved you?

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.250
Yes. He asked this of me...

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.870
Nerima-san, I'd like you to assist me
with some particular business.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.330
What business?

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.370
Look here.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:41.850
SCM Masters:
I have a proposal.
I will buy your slaves from you
at the following prices.
Teenage Girl.......... 25 million

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:41.850
20-24 y/o.......... 15 million
25-34 y/o.......... 10 million
35+.......... 5 million

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.450
I merely thought many things were possible
by your name alone.

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.370
Thank you for your consideration.
Muon Group
Muon Nerima

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:47.160
His idea was to buy and sell slaves.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:51.160
We'd buy slaves, then I would sell them
on the black market.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.500
I understand your thinking,

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:59.330
but do you really think masters
will just come to us to sell their slaves?

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:03.040
True, they won't come to sell on their own volition.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.160
You need not worry, however.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:10.000
All you need to do is steal away the slaves
of those who come to challenge you.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.540
With my Judgement SCM, of course.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:17.540
Then, we won't need to pay them anything
to get their slaves.

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:23.290
I get data on SCMs, and you get money.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:26.040
Everyone benefits.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:29.540
Let me give you some brand-new SCMs.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.250
Please pass these out to any lively youths you know.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.660
As the SCMs spread through society,
the number of slaves will grow,

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.700
bringing us more business.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:44.790
He tricked Minami in order to get closer to me.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.000
What a disgusting man.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.290
Just as I thought.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.830
Figure something out?

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:54.040
Setagaya's just stealing slaves from other people.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:58.330
If he really was invincible, he could
just go around challenging people to duels.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.830
That's true.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:03.370
He's being discreet and operating indirectly.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.500
But as it stands, we can't even get close to him,
let alone duel him.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.540
Sorry I'm late!

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.040
Time is money, Minami.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.330
Shut it, Old Man!

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.540
Hey, that gal chick isn't here.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:21.790
You're right...

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:26.750
Oh my god...

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:27.790
What?

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:33.450
Sachi-san?!

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.620
To Eia Arakawa.
I've captured Sachi Shibuya.
This is a declaration of war.
Come to the Higure Warehouse #9
at midnight tonight. We'll be waiting.
-Tsubaki Setagaya

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.870
"I've captured Sachi Shibuya.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.870
declaration of war

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.870
This is a declaration of war."

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.950
Come to the Higure Warehouse #9
at midnight tonight. We'll be waiting.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:44.410
Tsubaki Setagaya.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:48.540
That bastard, is he watching us
through some kinda camera or something?

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.450
Eia, we just talked about
how we shouldn't get close to Setagaya

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:57.790
when we don't know anything
about the Judgement SCM.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.330
I know.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:00.370
Nerima-san.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:04.160
What would you do with someone you'd captured?

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:07.160
Well, that's a horrific question...

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:12.160
But she's an important card in my hand,
so I'd keep her locked up till the meetup happened.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:17.790
We might be able to take Sachi-san back
if we find out where she's locked up before the meetup.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:20.290
Hey now, how the hell are we gonna find her?

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.290
Wait, seriously?

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:24.410
Will you help us?

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:28.660
Of course, I'd do anything for you, Eia-chan.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:32.000
Girls like you are totally my type.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.290
Christ, you're creepy, Old Man.

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:51.290
Don't move, Yuuga Ohta.

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:53.580
Where's Eia Arakawa?

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:58.620
It's a trap!

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:08.080
We've secured Warehouse #9, Mr. Nerima.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.540
Setagaya is inside.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:13.450
Eia-chan, everything's going according to plan.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.410
Thank you, especially for getting your men to help.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.410
Save the thanks for later, Eia.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.160
We've got to get this done quick.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:30.000
This is the one.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:32.660
Let's go while we've got the chance.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.410
Sachi-san!

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.200
We're here to save you!

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.500
S-somewhere on those shelves...

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.410
...is the key to these locks.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.410
Got it, hold tight.

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:52.200
Let's split up to search.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:54.790
I'm sorry!

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:10.000
It was a goddamn trap.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.750
My, my, it seems you've fallen right into my trap.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.200
Tsubaki Setagaya!

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:20.080
You did a wonderful job leading them into it,
just as I ordered you, Sachi Shibuya-san.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:24.040
Why are you here?

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:28.540
What? I just used the same trick you did.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:33.790
The person in that warehouse alley
was Meguro in disguise.

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:35.160
You knew what we were gonna do...

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:40.410
Oh, is that you, Zushiohmaru?

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:42.500
I didn't know you were with them.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.910
This does save me time in capturing you.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:50.910
Speaking of which, I don't see your master, Eia Arakawa.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:57.790
Well, that's alright. It just means
I've let a single ant get away from me.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:08:58.910
Dammit...

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.040
Eia!

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.290
Run!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.290
You're my insurance, remember?

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:33.370
What?! But why?

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.330
We were working with her all this time...

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:36.540
What's up?

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:39.450
Mr. Nerima just told us to capture Eia-san!

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.160
Yuuga Ohta

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.580
Ryuuou Edogawa and Eia Arakawa...

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:14.950
You've destroyed both of those huge groups
in the blink of an eye.

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:19.250
Everything is going according to your plans.

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:22.580
It's all thanks to your help, Fujiko-san.

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:25.160
You are so very intelligent.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:28.700
I hope you will continue to be
one of my greatest allies from now on.

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:32.700
Tsubaki
Setagaya

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:35.330
I'd be honored.

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:46.870
Still, that Judgement SCM of yours
is truly incredible. It's invincible.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.410
Have you heard of Pavlov's dogs?

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.540
Pavlov's dogs...

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:56.950
That was the experiment where he rang a bell
just before each time the dogs were fed,

00:10:56.950 --> 00:11:01.370
and eventually, the sound of the bell alone
would cause the dogs to salivate.

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.700
Classical conditioning, correct?

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:05.160
What about it?

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:17.120
The Judgement SCM triggers and amplifies the signals
of a duel start and a duel loss in other SCMs.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:23.620
This creates a false sense of a game starting
and a game concluding.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:30.410
The SCM needs the realization of losing a game
to operate on its user.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.620
If the user has never felt that realization of loss,

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:38.160
then the false sensation of a game concluding
would mean nothing to them.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:45.160
However, those who have lost a game
possess strong memories of that moment.

00:11:45.410 --> 00:11:51.370
When their brains receive the signal from
the Judgement SCM, they flash back to those memories,

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:55.040
which recreates the realization of loss within them.

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:59.120
I see. Just as the ringing of the bell
was enough to cause salivation in those dogs.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:04.330
the signal from the SCM is enough
to make the brain think that it's lost.

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:08.450
But that means that someone
who has never lost to another wouldn't...

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:09.580
That's right.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:16.580
Unfortunately, the Judgement SCM only works
on those who have been enslaved before.

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:21.790
However, if I continue to improve upon it
using the samples I've collected...

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:27.830
It seems I've had too much to drink.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:29.160
Excuse me.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:29.950
Of course.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:48.580
The Judgement SCM merely re-uses
the SCM functions that Sumida invented.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:55.040
But to create those signals in other SCMs,
it amplifies those signals within my own brain.

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.120
That burden weighs heavily upon me...

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:00.870
I'm collecting more and more behavioral samples.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:03.330
I just need a few more...

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:17.290
Wh-who are you?

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:28.160
Even the toilet water sounds fancy as fuck
in this expensive hotel.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:38.830
C'mon, let's duel, Tsubaki-sensei.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:50.580
S-stop!

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:57.120
Made your choice?

00:13:57.120 --> 00:14:00.370
At this rate, you won't even be able
to wear your SCM anymore.

00:14:00.370 --> 00:14:02.620
Please, stop...

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:04.080
I'll duel you.

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:08.330
He's got an SCM that I haven't enslaved yet...

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:10.250
Takio Minato...

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:13.080
I never thought he'd do something this bold...

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:17.620
I need to wear my SCM to duel you.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.250
If I can steal his slaves with my Judgement SCM...

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.580
Just so you know,
your Judgement SCM won't work on us.

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:30.160
They're not wearing SCMs, and I've never lost.

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:33.080
How do you know about that?

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:39.330
The duel will be a lie-guessing game.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:43.370
I'm going to give you statements,
and you pick which one's the lie.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:47.830
If you get it wrong even once, you lose. Sound good?

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.080
Yeah.

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:52.000
Let's begin!

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.290
Let's start with introductions.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:59.620
I'm Takio Minato. I bought my SCM online.

00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:05.120
What? You can ask me questions if you want.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:08.250
Are you with Eia Arakawa?

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:11.870
Nope. She stole one of my slaves.

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:14.540
How did you know where I was?

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.370
Well, that was easy.

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:23.950
Fujiko-san!

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:26.620
They're the enemy! Help me, quickly!

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:32.410
Fujiko's the one who told us all your info.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:37.040
Your location, the rules of your SCM, everything!

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.700
You never realized it?

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:42.000
Fujiko really had you hook, line, and sinker!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.500
Y-you're lying!

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.870
No, he's not.

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:55.000
Right now, I'm Takio Minato's slave.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:16:00.910
He approached me saying he was
Shinnosuke-sama's acquaintance.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:02.700
Isn't that awful?

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:05.660
You lose.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:09.120
Why...

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:12.410
You of all people should understand
the value of these things!

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:15.910
So why... for the stupidest reason, why?!

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:18.700
Well...

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.580
At the very least, he's of more value to me than you are.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:32.080
Cocky bastard... even after being
so totally fooled by his own slave.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:40.450
This is what happens to you
when you look down on people.

00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:48.220
Takio
Minato

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:50.470
Kabuki-cho Ichiban-machi

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.450
Her...

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:57.370
Them...

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.750
I wish I could make all of them mine...

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:05.500
Excuse me, Sir!

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:08.790
How about a night with one of our girls?

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:13.000
Right now, our number one girl's available,
and I could take you right to her!

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.120
I-I'm good.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.120
Right now, our number one girl's available,
and I could take you right to her!

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:15.000
Right now, our number one girl's available,
and I could take you right to her!

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.250
How about it?

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:17.950
I told you, I'm good!

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.120
How about a night with one of our girls?

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:30.750
Fuck, fuck, fuck!

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.450
Fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck!

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:36.000
Every fucking one of looks down on me!

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:38.750
If this is real...

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:45.250
This SCM can turn people into your slaves,
or so that shady site was saying.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:49.950
I won the auction, and read that
long-ass instruction manual, too.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.700
But it hasn't gone off at all!

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:53.910
Hey, Takio?

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:57.200
Yeah, it is you!

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:58.830
What're you up to?

00:17:58.830 --> 00:17:59.500
If you're free, come hang with me, I'll even pay.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.450
If you're free, come hang with me, I'll even pay.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:01.450
He's that guy from work... that dork.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:04.080
He's that guy from work... that dork.

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:06.330
You really gonna cover me?

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:09.580
Yeah! I just won big at slots.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:11.160
Welcome!

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:13.580
Umm, is Julia-chan here?

00:18:15.580 --> 00:18:18.080
So that's the hostess he's after.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:22.410
What, is he trying to tell me that I'm so little of a threat,
he can even take me to see his favorite hostess?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.200
My SCM went off...

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:30.330
Hello! I'm Julia.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:32.620
I'm Sachi.

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:37.120
Are they wearing SCMs?

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:39.000
Nice to meet you.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.450
Yeah, even that last event!

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:49.750
No exclusives at all.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:51.200
Yeah, I know!

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:53.500
What? I wasn't talking to you.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:57.330
Hey, I've got it!

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:00.040
Why don't we all play a game?
How about it, Sachi-san?

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:04.500
Oh, uh, let's see, then...

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.290
Why won't we play Daifugo?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.870
Hey, that's a nice idea.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.290
Really?

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.500
Yeah, alright! Let's do it!

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.200
I ain't gonna lose, y'hear!

00:19:16.200 --> 00:19:17.910
Let's begin.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:21.370
Ugh, I lose!

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:39.290
Jeez, why'd it have to be you, and not Julia?

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:44.120
Still, you did a good job saying we should play Daifugo!

00:19:45.290 --> 00:19:47.580
As a reward, hmm...

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:52.500
I'll let you give all the money you make at the club to me!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.160
Got it?!

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:55.450
Yes, Sir...

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:57.660
The SCM was the real deal.

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:00.830
I captured my first slave, Sachi.

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:07.120
But after a while, even Sachi started to ignore me.

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:09.290
God dammit, Yuuga...

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:18.040
Sorry there. You alright?

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:20.040
I wasn't lookin' where I was goin'.

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:21.200
Don't touch that!

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:22.950
Hey!

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.040
Fuck, fuck!

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.660
Fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck, fuck!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.500
Every fucking one of them looks down on me!

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:31.830
Makes fun of me!

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.830
Thinks nothing of me!

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.500
But I've got power now!

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:39.330
I've got the power to enslave you all!

00:20:39.750 --> 00:20:42.700
The invincible power of the SCM!

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:51.790
I kept watching the map,
and found a bunch of people with SCMs.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.540
The first one I went after was Maria Chiyoda.

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:58.290
Why her first? She seemed like the easiest target.

00:20:58.500 --> 00:21:02.330
Next, I got info from Zero Shinagawa...

00:21:02.830 --> 00:21:05.830
Excuse me, I'd like to ask you about Shinnosuke-san...

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:09.080
...I got Fujiko Taito to be my slave.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:13.330
As soon as I said his name,
she was completely on my side.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.450
And now...

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:19.330
Tsubaki and all his slaves are mine.

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:24.580
That's right. As long as you have
the captured slaves equip their SCMs,

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:27.700
you will become the master of eighteen slaves.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.700
Eighteen at once?!

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.830
It's a total upheaval!

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:36.330
Do you know the game Daifugo?

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:40.450
I'm real good at making the weakest card
into the strongest one!

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:42.950
Hey, Tsubaki.

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:46.250
Does anyone have more slaves than me right now?

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.200
No, you have the most.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:51.750
Suck it, Assholes!

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:55.370
I'm the best... I'm number one!

00:22:17.330 --> 00:22:20.950
-harvest-

00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:27.660
The ultimate game is testing my heart

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:32.450
A strategy that starts from a one-on-one

00:22:32.450 --> 00:22:35.120
It's getting close, do I attack or pull back

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:36.910
Play defense or offense on the brink?

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:40.040
Tell me, which is better?

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:44.290
I don't care if the rules leave me without a chance

00:22:44.290 --> 00:22:50.500
I have one last chance in my hand for my unclear future

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:55.660
Does the deck in front of me shine light on that future?

00:22:56.330 --> 00:23:05.250
Examining your visible and hidden expression, my fate concealed

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:10.410
Drawing forth luck, I don't want to lose

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:14.160
I can't evolve if I keep saying "I can't"

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:18.790
I'll win my game with you

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:26.620
And overcome all barriers, so I never go bust again

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:45.410
-explosion-
